 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Real-Time Fraud Detection: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Problem Context & Objective\n",
    "In financial risk management and real-time transaction processing, fraud detection is characterized by:\n",
    "- **Extreme Class Imbalance**: Genuine transactions represent >99.8% of all volume; fraud accounts for <0.2%.\n",
    "- **Asymmetric Misclassification Costs**: A false negative (missing a \$5,000 unauthorized transaction) is substantially more detrimental than a false positive (triggering an automated SMS confirmation or temporary review).\n",
    "- **Evolving Adversarial Patterns**: Fraudsters continually adapt their techniques, creating non-stationary feature distributions and temporal drift.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook conducts a focused, rigorous exploratory data analysis to inspect the data quality, understand the class imbalance, analyze transaction amount distributions, and uncover correlation patterns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "# Styling\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid' if 'seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid' in plt.style.available else 'default')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 11\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10, 5)\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.data.loader import load_credit_card_data\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load dataset\n",
    "df = load_credit_card_data(data_path='../data/raw/creditcard.csv', auto_generate_if_missing=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset shape: {df.shape[0]:,} rows, {df.shape[1]} columns\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Dataset Overview & Data Quality Assessment\n",
    "We inspect data types, missing values, and duplicate records."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Missing value audit\n",
    "missing_counts = df.isnull().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Total missing values across all columns: {missing_counts.sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Duplicate rows audit\n",
    "duplicate_count = df.duplicated().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Total duplicate records: {duplicate_count:,} ({duplicate_count / len(df) * 100:.2f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Summary statistics for Time and Amount\n",
    "df[['Time', 'Amount']].describe().T"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Class Imbalance Analysis\n",
    "Demonstrating the extreme skew in the binary target `Class` (0 = Legitimate, 1 = Fraud)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class_counts = df['Class'].value_counts()\n",
    "fraud_rate = df['Class'].mean() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Legitimate Transactions (Class 0): {class_counts[0]:,} ({100 - fraud_rate:.3f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Fraudulent Transactions (Class 1): {class_counts[1]:,} ({fraud_rate:.3f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Imbalance Ratio: 1 fraud per {class_counts[0] // class_counts[1]:,} legitimate transactions\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bar chart with log scale\n",
    "sns.barplot(x=['Legitimate (0)', 'Fraud (1)'], y=[class_counts[0], class_counts[1]], ax=ax[0], palette=['#2b5c8f', '#d9534f'])\n",
    "ax[0].set_yscale('log')\n",
    "ax[0].set_title('Transaction Volume by Class (Log Scale)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax[0].set_ylabel('Transaction Count (Log Scale)')\n",
    "for i, count in enumerate([class_counts[0], class_counts[1]]):\n",
    "    ax[0].text(i, count * 1.2, f\"{count:,}\", ha='center', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Donut chart\n",
    "ax[1].pie([class_counts[0], class_counts[1]], labels=['Legitimate', 'Fraud'], autopct='%1.2f%%',\n",
    "          startangle=90, colors=['#2b5c8f', '#d9534f'], explode=(0, 0.2),\n",
    "          wedgeprops=dict(width=0.4, edgecolor='w'))\n",
    "ax[1].set_title('Target Class Distribution', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Transaction Amount Behavior: Fraud vs Legitimate\n",
    "Analyzing the distribution of transaction amounts between legitimate and fraudulent activities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Legitimate Amount Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(df[df['Class'] == 0]['Amount'].describe().round(2))\n",
    "print(\"\\nFraudulent Amount Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(df[df['Class'] == 1]['Amount'].describe().round(2))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Log-amount distribution\n",
    "sns.histplot(np.log1p(df[df['Class'] == 0]['Amount']), bins=40, kde=True, ax=ax[0], color='#2b5c8f', label='Legitimate', stat='density')\n",
    "sns.histplot(np.log1p(df[df['Class'] == 1]['Amount']), bins=40, kde=True, ax=ax[0], color='#d9534f', label='Fraud', stat='density')\n",
    "ax[0].set_title('Log-Transformed Transaction Amount Density (log1p)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax[0].set_xlabel('log(Amount + 1)')\n",
    "ax[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Boxplot (capped for visual clarity)\n",
    "sns.boxplot(data=df, x='Class', y='Amount', ax=ax[1], palette=['#2b5c8f', '#d9534f'], showfliers=False)\n",
    "ax[1].set_xticklabels(['Legitimate (0)', 'Fraud (1)'])\n",
    "ax[1].set_title('Amount Distribution Comparison (Outliers hidden)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Temporal Patterns: Time-of-Day Dynamics\n",
    "Analyzing whether fraudulent transactions exhibit distinct temporal behavior (e.g. nocturnal activity)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert elapsed seconds to hour of day (0 to 23)\n",
    "df['Hour_of_Day'] = ((df['Time'] / 3600) % 24).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "hourly_counts = df.groupby(['Hour_of_Day', 'Class']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
    "hourly_fraud_rate = hourly_counts[1] / (hourly_counts[0] + hourly_counts[1]) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "ax2 = ax1.twinx()\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.bar(hourly_counts.index, hourly_counts[0], alpha=0.4, color='#2b5c8f', label='Legitimate Count (Left Axis)')\n",
    "ax2.plot(hourly_fraud_rate.index, hourly_fraud_rate, color='#d9534f', marker='o', linewidth=2.5, label='Fraud Rate % (Right Axis)')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Hour of Day (0-23)', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Legitimate Transaction Count', color='#2b5c8f', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('Fraud Rate (%)', color='#d9534f', fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.title('Transaction Volume and Hourly Fraud Rate Throughout the Day', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Correlation with Fraud Target\n",
    "Examining the correlation of PCA features with the target variable `Class` to identify key risk drivers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "corr = df.corr()['Class'].drop(['Class', 'Hour_of_Day']).sort_values()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "colors = ['#d9534f' if c < 0 else '#2b5c8f' for c in corr.values]\n",
    "corr.plot(kind='bar', color=colors, ax=ax)\n",
    "plt.title('Feature Correlations with Fraud Target (Class)', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Pearson Correlation Coefficient')\n",
    "plt.axhline(0, color='black', linestyle='--', linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Top 5 Negatively Correlated Features:\")\n",
    "print(corr.head(5))\n",
    "print(\"\\nTop 5 Positively Correlated Features:\")\n",
    "print(corr.tail(5))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Key Findings & Modeling Takeaways\n",
    "1. **Severe Imbalance**: With a fraud rate under 0.2%, Accuracy is completely meaningless (a naive classifier predicting all 0s achieves 99.8% accuracy with 0% recall). We must optimize for **PR-AUC, Recall, Precision, and Cost**.\n",
    "2. **Amount Skew**: Transaction amount is heavily right-skewed. Log transformation `log1p(Amount)` and robust standardization are mandatory.\n",
    "3. **Strong Discriminative Latent Signals**: Several PCA components (V14, V10, V12, V17 negatively correlated, V4, V11 positively correlated) provide strong non-linear signal separation.\n",
    "4. **Temporal Seasonality**: Diurnal variation and velocity spikes suggest that cyclical time features (sin/cos encoding of hour of day) and rolling velocity windows will enrich model discriminative capacity."
   ]
  }
 ],
